<title>GERMANY: RWE ends telecoms alliance with BT, VIAG.</title>
<headline>RWE ends telecoms alliance with BT, VIAG.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>German utility RWE AG said on Wednesday it was pulling out of a German telecoms alliance with British Telecom and Viag AG due to differences over market strategy.</p>
<p>RWE said in a regulatory news announcement it was in the final stage of negotiations with Veba AG and Cable &amp; Wireless on &quot;taking a new direction to enter the German telecommunications market&quot;.</p>
<p>Veba also said earlier that the three-way talks were nearing completion.</p>
<p>RWE said, however, it would continue to cooperate with Viag in the area of telecoms infrastructure.</p>
<p>-- Douglas Busvine, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
